IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-fees-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-fees-draft`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-made`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-amended`

-- g8-fees.l4: the Fees Regulations across their three vintages.
--
-- The vintage is an INPUT of every function here.  A vintage that is silent on a service answers silence (NOTHING),
-- never a figure from another vintage; a vintage that is not visible (regulations 3 to 5 of the draft) answers a
-- named refusal.  The three vintage modules say what each text prints; this module chooses among them, applies
-- regulation 3 (update of fees) and regulation 4 (payment as a condition) to the choice, and says which vintage is in
-- force on a day.  It reads no section of the Law that another group decides: what the Law needs from here is
-- the entry into force of the s.59 regulations (IP13) and the fee-paid test of regulation 4 (IP11), both exported.
--
-- Headline functions, all marked @export:
--   the amount the Fees Regulations state in the vintage for the service           (the printed figure; NOTHING if silent)
--   the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day   (the figure after regulation 3's updates)
--   regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage                           (the fee-paid test of IP11)
--   the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on                 (IP13)

§ `Section 59 of the Law: the heads of fee`

-- src:439 | {{ח:סעיף|59|אגרות}}
-- src:440 | {{ח:ת}} השר, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע אגרות בעד הגשת בקשה לרישיון, בעד מתן רישיון או חידושו, בעד בחינות הנדרשות לקבלת תעודת גמר ובכלל זה השגה על בחינות, ובעד השתלמויות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 17|סעיף 17}}; בתקנות כאמור רשאי השר לקבוע שיעורי אגרה שונים בעד הגשת בקשה לרישיון זמני למומחה זר או לחידושו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 9|סעיף 9}} ובעד מתן רישיון זמני כאמור.
-- Paraphrase (mine; the Hebrew governs): the Minister, with the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare
-- Committee, may fix fees for submitting an application for a licence, for giving a licence or renewing it, for the
-- exams required to obtain a final certificate, including an objection to exams, and for training courses under
-- section 17; and in such regulations he may fix different rates for submitting an application for a temporary
-- licence for a foreign expert, or renewing it, under section 9, and for giving a temporary licence.
-- The nine constructors of `Service under the Fees Regulations` are these heads, kept separate: the draft prices
-- the APPLICATION for a licence, the text as made prices its RECEIPT (the heads are distinct in s.59), and no vintage
-- prices the grant of a temporary licence or a section 17 course.  A head a vintage does not price answers NOTHING.
@ref Law s.59 (src:439-440)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `, for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN `the SimpLEX draft states, for the service` service
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN `the Fees Regulations as made state, for the service` service
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN `the Fees Regulations as amended state, for the service` service

@ref Law s.59 (src:439-440)
@export The figure, in new shekels, that one text of the Fees Regulations (the SimpLEX draft, as made, or as amended) prints for a service, before any update under regulation 3; nothing at all where that text fixes no fee for the service
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc Which text: the SimpLEX draft, the regulations as made (9 July 2025) or as amended (4 May 2026)
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc What is charged for: an application, a licence, a temporary licence, an exam, an objection or a training course
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `, for the service` service
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee THEN JUST (fee's `the amount stated`)

@ref Law s.59 (src:439-440)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the provision that states the fee in` vintage `for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `, for the service` service
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee THEN JUST (fee's `the provision that states it`)

@ref Law s.59 (src:439-440)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Payer under the Fees Regulations`
`the payer the Fees Regulations name in` vintage `for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `, for the service` service
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee THEN fee's `the payer the provision names`

@ref Law s.59 (src:439-440)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vintage is silent on the service` vintage `, the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `, for the service` service
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST fee THEN FALSE

§ `Regulation 5 and the amending regulations: when each vintage came into force`

-- src:460 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} תחילתו של חוק זה, למעט {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק ו׳}} –
-- src:461 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר דליק המנוי {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|בתוספת הרביעית}}, ובלבד שהשימוש בו הותר על פי כל דין – שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, לפי המאוחר (להלן – יום התחילה); השר, לאחר התייעצות עם השר להגנת הסביבה, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|התוספת הרביעית}};
-- src:462 | {{ח:תתת}} {{ח:הערה|(תחילתן של התקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, היא ביום 16.7.2025).}}
-- Paraphrase (mine; the Hebrew governs): s.63(a)(1) takes, as one limb of the commencement day, "the day the
-- regulations under section 59 enter into force".  The wiki's note says that day is 16.7.2025.
-- The regulations under section 59 are the Fees Regulations as made; the amendment of 2026 is not a regulation
-- under section 59 that fixes the day.  IP13 (G7 consumes it): 16.7.2025.
-- NOTE FOR G7: the words "three months from the day of its publication or the day the regulations enter into force,
-- whichever is later" can be read as the later of two dates, or as three months from the later date.  This group
-- exports the regulations' date and does not decide which; see FRAGMENT-G8.md.
@ref Law s.63(a)(1) (src:460-462); Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5
@export The day the Fees Regulations made under section 59 of the Law entered into force: seven days from their publication on 9 July 2025
GIVETH A DATE
`the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on` MEANS
    `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5; Fees (Amendment) Regulations 5786-2026
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the Fees Regulations came into force, in` vintage MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN JUST `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN JUST `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on`

-- The vintage in force on a day: none before 16.7.2025, the text as made from then to 3.5.2026, the text as
-- amended from 4.5.2026.  The draft is never in force.  A day-level answer: on 16.7.2025 and 4.5.2026 it answers
-- for the whole day, although IL s.21 binds each from 00:01 (the moment-level function below).
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5; Fees (Amendment) Regulations 5786-2026
@export Which text of the Fees Regulations is in force on a day: none before 16 July 2025, the text as made until 3 May 2026, the text as amended from 4 May 2026
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A MAYBE `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
`the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` day MEANS
    BRANCH IF day AT LEAST `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on`
                THEN JUST `the Fees Regulations as amended`
           IF day AT LEAST `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
                THEN JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5; Fees (Amendment) Regulations 5786-2026; Interpretation Law s 21
GIVEN m IS A Moment
GIVETH A MAYBE `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
`the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force at the moment` m MEANS
    BRANCH IF `s 21 — the moment` m `is one at which a statute commencing on` (`the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on`) `binds`
                THEN JUST `the Fees Regulations as amended`
           IF `s 21 — the moment` m `is one at which a statute commencing on` (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`) `binds`
                THEN JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Regulations 2 and 3: the fee payable on a day`

-- The sources hold no index reading and no notice under regulation 3(b).  The fee payable on a day before the
-- first update day is the printed figure; on or after it, the printed figure as updated, which needs the readings,
-- and without them is a named refusal, returned and never stored.

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the SimpLEX draft was never in force, so no fee is payable under it on any day` MEANS
    REFUSE "the SimpLEX draft was never in force, so no fee is payable under it on any day"

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a)
GIVEN readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
`the inputs of regulation 3 under the reading the encoding takes, with the readings` readings MEANS
    `Inputs of regulation 3` WITH
        `index readings` IS readings
        `the regulations came into force on` IS `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
        `the reading of regulation 3` IS `the reading of regulation 3 that the encoding takes`
        `notices of the Director General` IS EMPTY

-- The fee payable in a vintage for a service on a day.  Before the vintage came into force: NOTHING (no fee was
-- payable under it).  A service the vintage does not price: NOTHING.  Otherwise the printed figure, updated by
-- regulation 3(a) for every update day from the first that applies to it up to the day.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2 and regulation 3(a); Law s.59
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      day IS A DATE
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fee payable in` vintage `for the service` service `on the day` day `, under` ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN
        `the SimpLEX draft was never in force, so no fee is payable under it on any day`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN `the fee once the vintage is in force`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN `the fee once the vintage is in force`
    WHERE
        `the fee once the vintage is in force` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the Fees Regulations came into force, in` vintage
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST inForce THEN
                IF   day LESS THAN inForce
                THEN NOTHING
                ELSE `the updated fee`
        `the updated fee` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `, for the service` service
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST fee THEN JUST (`regulation 3(a) — the amount of the stated fee` fee `on the day` day `after the updates, under` ctx)

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2 and regulation 3(a); Law s.59
@export The fee the Fees Regulations fix for a service on a day, in one text of the regulations, after the yearly updates of regulation 3; nothing where the text fixes no fee or was not yet in force; a refusal where an update needs an index reading that was not supplied or the text is the SimpLEX draft
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc Which text: the SimpLEX draft (never in force), the regulations as made (9 July 2025) or as amended (4 May 2026)
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc What is charged for
      day IS A DATE @desc The day for which the fee is asked; the sources do not say whether this is the day of the application, the payment or the service
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc Every reading of the consumer price index you hold, with the day it was published; the sources give none, and without the two readings an update needs the answer is a refusal
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` MEANS
    `the fee payable in` vintage `for the service` service `on the day` day `, under` (`the inputs of regulation 3 under the reading the encoding takes, with the readings` readings)

§ `Regulation 2(b): what an objection costs`

-- "In addition to the payment of the fee as stated in sub-regulation (a)": the objection charge alone (taken, which
-- is what the SimpLEX row expects), the exam's own fee and then the charge, or, literally, the fee of whichever
-- sub-regulation (a) is.  In the draft, (a) is the theoretical fee even where the appeal concerns the practical exam;
-- as made it is the practical fee; as amended the text says (a1), the theoretical fee.

-- The sitting whose fee the objection text cross-refers to, as the vintage's own numbering has it.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b); Fees Regulations as amended, regulation 2(b); SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
`the sitting whose fee the objection text cross-refers to, in` vintage MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN `the service of sitting a practical exam`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b); Fees Regulations as amended, regulation 2(b); SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c)
GIVEN service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Service under the Fees Regulations`
`the sitting of the exam objected to by the objection` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` THEN JUST `the service of sitting a practical exam`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` THEN JUST `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The amount due from an objector for n objections, given how the fee of a service is looked up (the printed figure,
-- or the figure payable on a day).  NOTHING if the vintage fixes no charge for the objection, or if the reading
-- needs the fee of a sitting that the vintage does not fix.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b); Fees Regulations as amended, regulation 2(b); SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c)
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the objection charge`
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      n IS A NUMBER
      feeOf IS A FUNCTION FROM `Service under the Fees Regulations` TO MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount due, reading the objection charge as` reading `, in` vintage `for the objection` service `, the number of objections` n `, the fees being` feeOf MEANS
    CONSIDER feeOf service
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST charge THEN
        CONSIDER reading
        WHEN `the objection charge alone` THEN JUST (charge TIMES n)
        WHEN `the fee of the exam objected to and the objection charge` THEN
            CONSIDER `the sitting of the exam objected to by the objection` service
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST sitting THEN `the exam fee plus the charges` sitting charge
        WHEN `the fee that the cross-referenced sub-regulation states and the objection charge` THEN
            `the exam fee plus the charges` (`the sitting whose fee the objection text cross-refers to, in` vintage) charge
    WHERE
        `the exam fee plus the charges` sitting charge MEANS
            CONSIDER feeOf sitting
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST examFee THEN JUST (examFee PLUS (charge TIMES n))

-- At the printed figures: no day, no update.  The only level the draft can answer at.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b); Fees Regulations as amended, regulation 2(b); SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c)
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the objection charge`
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the printed amount due, reading the objection charge as` reading `, in` vintage `for the objection` service `, the number of objections` n MEANS
    `the amount due, reading the objection charge as` reading `, in` vintage `for the objection` service `, the number of objections` n `, the fees being` printed
    WHERE
        printed s MEANS `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `for the service` s

-- On a day, with the updates of regulation 3(a).
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b) and regulation 3(a); Fees Regulations as amended, regulation 2(b)
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the objection charge`
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      n IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount due on the day, reading the objection charge as` reading `, in` vintage `for the objection` service `, the number of objections` n `, on the day` day `, under` ctx MEANS
    `the amount due, reading the objection charge as` reading `, in` vintage `for the objection` service `, the number of objections` n `, the fees being` payable
    WHERE
        payable s MEANS `the fee payable in` vintage `for the service` s `on the day` day `, under` ctx

§ `Regulation 4: payment as a condition`

-- The official regulation 4 binds for a service.  The first limb binds the Registrar as to giving or renewing a
-- licence; the second binds the Training Division as to the exams and the objection.  An application for an
-- ordinary licence and a continuing training course are not mentioned by regulation 4.
-- A temporary licence is the fork: its fee (2(d)) is fixed for the APPLICATION, and the first limb speaks of "a
-- licence for which a fee was fixed".  Taken: the fee fixed for the application binds the grant (purpose: the
-- grant of a licence is the end of an application whose fee is unpaid), whether the Registrar is asked about the
-- application or about the grant itself.  Alternative: only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant,
-- and no vintage fixes one.  (The first version of this module found no fee when asked about the GRANT of the
-- temporary licence and left the Registrar free; an independent test author found it, and `the service whose fee
-- regulation 4 looks at` is the repair.)
-- src:fees:38 | {{ח:ת}} הרשם לא ייתן רישיון שנקבעה בעדו אגרה לפי תקנות אלה ולא יחדשו, וכן האגף להכשרה מקצועית לא יאפשר ביצוע של הבחינות הנדרשות או הגשת השגה על בחינות, שנקבעה בעדן אגרה לפי תקנות אלה, אלא אם כן מבקש הרישיון או השירות כאמור שילם את האגרה במלואה לפי תקנות אלה.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4 (src:fees:38)
GIVEN r4 IS A `Reading of regulation 4`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` THEN JUST `the Registrar`
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` THEN
        CONSIDER r4's `a temporary licence`
        WHEN `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence` THEN JUST `the Registrar`
        WHEN `only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` THEN JUST `the Registrar`
    WHEN `the service of sitting a practical exam` THEN JUST `the Training Division`
    WHEN `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` THEN JUST `the Training Division`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` THEN JUST `the Training Division`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` THEN JUST `the Training Division`
    WHEN `the service of attending a continuing training course` THEN NOTHING

-- The service whose fee regulation 4 looks at.  For the grant of a temporary licence, under the taken reading, it is
-- the application for it, whose fee 2(d) fixes; for every other service it is the service itself.  (For an
-- ordinary licence the text as made and as amended price the RECEIPT of the licence, which is the grant, so the
-- service is its own: there is no gap there; see FRAGMENT-G8.md.)
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, first limb: "a licence for which a fee was fixed" (src:fees:38)
GIVEN r4 IS A `Reading of regulation 4`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
`the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` THEN
        CONSIDER r4's `a temporary licence`
        WHEN `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence` THEN
            `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
        WHEN `only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant` THEN service
    OTHERWISE service

-- A fee is fixed for the service in the vintage on the day: the vintage is in force and prices the service.  Read off
-- the printed figure, so that no index reading is needed to say that a fee exists.  (The draft is never in force.)
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4 (src:fees:38)
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a fee is fixed under the Fees Regulations in` vintage `for the service` service `on the day` day MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Fees Regulations came into force, in` vintage
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST inForce THEN
            day AT LEAST inForce
        AND NOT `the vintage is silent on the service` vintage `, the service` service

-- The facts regulation 4 asks about, for a service in a vintage, given what the payer paid.  Where the vintage fixes
-- no fee for the service, the bar speaks of "a service for which a fee was fixed" and none was: taken, the bar is
-- not engaged (nothing is owed, so nothing is outstanding); the alternative refuses to say.
-- The draft's regulation 4 is not visible: a refusal.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4 (src:fees:38)
GIVEN r4 IS A `Reading of regulation 4`
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      paid IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
`the facts regulation 4 asks about, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, in` vintage `for the service` service `, the payer having paid` paid `on the day` day `, under` ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN `the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN `the facts once regulation 4 is visible`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN `the facts once regulation 4 is visible`
    WHERE
        feeService MEANS `the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` service
        `the facts once regulation 4 is visible` MEANS
            IF   `a fee is fixed under the Fees Regulations in` vintage `for the service` feeService `on the day` day
            THEN `Facts regulation 4 asks about` WITH
                     `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS TRUE
                     `the payer paid the fee in full` IS `the payer paid in full`
            ELSE `the facts where no fee is fixed`
        -- A payer who paid nothing has not paid in full a fee fixed at a positive figure: the printed figures are positive
        -- and an update multiplies them by a positive factor (the positive readings the guard of regulation 3 demands),
        -- so no index reading is needed to say so.  Anyone who paid something needs the updated figure.
        `the payer paid in full` MEANS
            CONSIDER r4's `nothing was paid`
            WHEN `a payer who paid nothing has not paid in full, whatever the update` THEN
                IF   paid AT MOST 0
                THEN FALSE
                ELSE `the payment reaches the due figure`
            WHEN `the updated figure decides even where nothing was paid` THEN `the payment reaches the due figure`
        `the payment reaches the due figure` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the fee payable in` vintage `for the service` feeService `on the day` day `, under` ctx
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 4 found a fee fixed for the service and no figure payable for it`
            WHEN JUST due THEN `the payment is in full` due
        `the facts where no fee is fixed` MEANS
            CONSIDER r4's `a service with no fee`
            WHEN `regulation 4 is not engaged` THEN
                `Facts regulation 4 asks about` WITH
                    `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS FALSE
                    `the payer paid the fee in full` IS TRUE
            WHEN `regulation 4 refuses to say` THEN
                `regulation 4 speaks of a service for which a fee was fixed, and this text of the regulations fixes none for the service`
        `the payment is in full` due MEANS
            CONSIDER r4's `payment in full`
            WHEN `a payment of at least the fee is payment in full` THEN paid AT LEAST due
            WHEN `only a payment of exactly the fee is payment in full` THEN paid EQUALS due

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 4 speaks of a service for which a fee was fixed, and this text of the regulations fixes none for the service` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 4 speaks of a service for which a fee was fixed, and this text of the regulations fixes none for the service"

-- Not reachable on the printed figures: a fee that is fixed has a figure payable.  Named so that, were it ever
-- reached, it would say so.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 4 found a fee fixed for the service and no figure payable for it` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 4 found a fee fixed for the service and no figure payable for it"

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4 (src:fees:38)
GIVEN r4 IS A `Reading of regulation 4`
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
      paid IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, in` vintage `for the service` service `, the payer having paid` paid `on the day` day `, under` ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN `the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN `the bar once regulation 4 is visible`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN `the bar once regulation 4 is visible`
    WHERE
        `the bar once regulation 4 is visible` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` service
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST official THEN
                `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service`
                    (`the facts regulation 4 asks about, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, in` vintage `for the service` service `, the payer having paid` paid `on the day` day `, under` ctx)

-- The reading of regulation 4 that the encoding takes, and one value for each alternative.
GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 4`
`the reading of regulation 4 that the encoding takes` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 4` WITH
        `a service with no fee` IS `regulation 4 is not engaged`
        `a temporary licence` IS `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence`
        `payment in full` IS `a payment of at least the fee is payment in full`
        `nothing was paid` IS `a payer who paid nothing has not paid in full, whatever the update`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 4`
`the reading of regulation 4 that refuses where no fee is fixed` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 4` WITH
        `a service with no fee` IS `regulation 4 refuses to say`
        `a temporary licence` IS `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence`
        `payment in full` IS `a payment of at least the fee is payment in full`
        `nothing was paid` IS `a payer who paid nothing has not paid in full, whatever the update`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 4`
`the reading of regulation 4 that binds a temporary licence only by a fee fixed for the licence` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 4` WITH
        `a service with no fee` IS `regulation 4 is not engaged`
        `a temporary licence` IS `only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant`
        `payment in full` IS `a payment of at least the fee is payment in full`
        `nothing was paid` IS `a payer who paid nothing has not paid in full, whatever the update`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 4`
`the reading of regulation 4 that wants exactly the fee` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 4` WITH
        `a service with no fee` IS `regulation 4 is not engaged`
        `a temporary licence` IS `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence`
        `payment in full` IS `only a payment of exactly the fee is payment in full`
        `nothing was paid` IS `a payer who paid nothing has not paid in full, whatever the update`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 4`
`the reading of regulation 4 that needs the updated figure even where nothing was paid` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 4` WITH
        `a service with no fee` IS `regulation 4 is not engaged`
        `a temporary licence` IS `the fee fixed for the application binds the grant of the temporary licence`
        `payment in full` IS `a payment of at least the fee is payment in full`
        `nothing was paid` IS `the updated figure decides even where nothing was paid`

-- The exported fee-paid test of IP11 (G1 and G2 take it as their `the fee was paid in full` input).  It answers
-- TRUE where regulation 4 leaves the service free: no fee is fixed, or the fee is paid in full.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4 (src:fees:38)
@export Whether regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations leaves a service free to go ahead: false where a fee is fixed for it and the payer has not paid that fee in full, true where no fee is fixed or the fee is paid; a refusal for the SimpLEX draft, whose regulation 4 is not visible, and where an update needs an index reading that was not supplied
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc Which text: the SimpLEX draft, the regulations as made or as amended
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc What is asked for: the licence, the temporary licence, an exam or an objection
      paid IS A NUMBER @desc The number of new shekels the payer has paid for the service
      day IS A DATE @desc The day for which the fee is asked
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc Every reading of the consumer price index you hold, with its publication day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` MEANS
    NOT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that the encoding takes`) `, in` vintage `for the service` service `, the payer having paid` paid `on the day` day `, under` (`the inputs of regulation 3 under the reading the encoding takes, with the readings` readings)

-- The two limbs of regulation 4 as the two officials' tests, which is how G1 and G2 (the Registrar) and the Training
-- Division consume it.  Each refuses if the service is not one the official acts on.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 4 binds the Registrar for licences only, and the service is not a licence` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 4 binds the Registrar for licences only, and the service is not a licence"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 4 binds the Training Division for exams and objections only, and the service is neither` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 4 binds the Training Division for exams and objections only, and the service is neither"

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, first limb (src:fees:38)
@export Whether regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations leaves the Registrar free to give or renew a licence, given what the applicant has paid: the licence or the temporary licence application is the service
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc Which text: the regulations as made or as amended (the draft's regulation 4 is not visible)
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc The licence being given or renewed, the grant of a foreign expert's temporary licence, or its application
      paid IS A NUMBER @desc New shekels the applicant has paid
      day IS A DATE @desc The day for which the fee is asked
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc Every reading of the consumer price index you hold, with its publication day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that the encoding takes`) `, the service` service
    WHEN JUST `the Registrar` THEN `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vintage service paid day readings
    OTHERWISE `regulation 4 binds the Registrar for licences only, and the service is not a licence`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, second limb (src:fees:38)
@export Whether regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations leaves the Training Division free to allow an exam or the lodging of an objection, given what the examinee or the objector has paid
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc Which text: the regulations as made or as amended (the draft's regulation 4 is not visible)
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc The exam sitting or the objection
      paid IS A NUMBER @desc New shekels the examinee or objector has paid
      day IS A DATE @desc The day for which the fee is asked
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc Every reading of the consumer price index you hold, with its publication day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that the encoding takes`) `, the service` service
    WHEN JUST `the Training Division` THEN `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vintage service paid day readings
    OTHERWISE `regulation 4 binds the Training Division for exams and objections only, and the service is neither`
